-- title:
--   Vélu's isogeny with kernel generated by a point of order N
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field with decidable equality, let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $F$ which is elliptic, and let $N$ be a nonzero natural number with $N \neq 0$ in $F$. Let $Q$ be a point of the affine model of $W$ whose additive order is exactly $N$. Write $\mathrm{coordsOrZero}$ for the map sending the point at infinity to $(0,0)$ and an affine point $(x,y)$ to $(x,y)$, and let $S = \{\mathrm{coordsOrZero}(kQ) : 1 \le k \le N-1\}$ as a finite subset of $F \times F$. The target curve `W.fullKernelQuotient Q N` has the same $a_1, a_2, a_3$ as $W$, while $a_4$ is replaced by $a_4 - 5t$ and $a_6$ by $a_6 - b_2 t - 7w$, where $t = \sum_{(x,y) \in S} (3x^2 + 2a_2 x + a_4 - a_1 y)$ and $w = \sum_{(x,y)\in S} \bigl(x(3x^2+2a_2x+a_4-a_1y) + y(2y+a_1x+a_3)\bigr)$. The assertion is that there exists an additive group homomorphism $\varphi$ from the points of $W$ to the points of this curve whose kernel is precisely the subgroup of integer multiples of $Q$, and such that for every point $P$ not a multiple of $Q$ the pair $\mathrm{coordsOrZero}(\varphi P)$ equals $$\Bigl(x_P + \sum_{k=1}^{N-1}\bigl(x_{P+kQ} - x_{kQ}\bigr),\; y_P + \sum_{k=1}^{N-1}\bigl(y_{P+kQ} - y_{kQ}\bigr)\Bigr),$$ the coordinates being taken via $\mathrm{coordsOrZero}$, so that a vanishing summand is contributed by any multiple that is the point at infinity.
--
--   This is Vélu's isogeny with kernel the cyclic group generated by $Q$, written uniformly in $N$ (all multiples of $Q$ entering the sums, whatever the parity of $N$) rather than over a half-system as in the classical odd-degree formulas; nonvanishing of the discriminant of the quotient curve is a separate statement. It is used in the treatment of modular curves, for instance in comparing moduli places under Atkin–Lehner involutions and under $q$-expansion, and in the computation of ramification indices.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_fullKernelHom.lean

import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_FullKernelQuotient

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
